Twice procedure for 4353eh non linear smoother                 [STB-11: sed7.2]
Version 1.0 for Stata 3.0
----------------------------------------------
             
	^smtwice^ datavar smthvar finsmth


Description
-----------

^smtwice^ calcules rough from 4253eh, smoothes rough values and add the result
to smthvar to produce finsmth (final smoothed values by 4253eh,twice).
^finrough^ is created to assess the model, ^timendx^ is created to serve as 
an index for the graph that appears on screen once the calculations have 
finished. The numerical results can be recalled by the list command.


Example
-------

 . ^smtwice raw smooth smootwce^

the graph of observed and smooth twiced values vs. timendx appears on screen

 . ^list^

the numerical results of the twicing are showed on screen


References
----------

Salgado-Ugarte, I. H., & J. Curts-García (1992) sed7: Resistant smoothing using 
         Stata. Stata Technical Bulletin 7: 8–11. Reimpreso en Stata Technical 
